########################################################################
#
# Format of Lines:
#
#   source/type destination/type cost filter
#
# General Notes:
#
#   The "cost" field is used to find the least costly filters to run
#   when converting a job file to a printable format.
#
#   All filters *must* accept the standard command-line arguments
#   (job-id, user, title, copies, options, [filename or stdin]) to
#   work with CUPS.
#
#   Presswork ships the scheduler and backends only. Conversion filters
#   such as `pstops`, `rastertopwg`, `pdftopdf`, and `pdftoraster` are
#   external executables supplied by the OpenPrinting `cups-filters`
#   package (install `cups-filters` on Linux if you print to non-driverless
#   printers or submit formats that require server-side rasterization).
#   Driverless IPP Everywhere / AirPrint printers accept PDF, PWG Raster,
#   and URF directly without legacy PPD filters.
#

########################################################################
#
# PostScript filters (provided by cups-filters)
#

application/postscript		application/vnd.cups-postscript	66	pstops

########################################################################
#
# Raster filters (provided by cups-filters)
#

# PWG Raster filter for IPP Everywhere...
application/vnd.cups-raster	image/pwg-raster		100	rastertopwg
application/vnd.cups-raster	image/urf			100	rastertopwg

########################################################################
#
# Raw passthrough filter
#
# Raw passthrough is enabled below by default so pre-formatted jobs and
# driverless clients can submit `application/octet-stream` without `-o raw`.
# Comment out the following line (or override via `local.convs`) to reject
# unrecognised binary data unless the client explicitly passes `-o raw`.
#

application/octet-stream	application/vnd.cups-raw	0	-
